@!internal

--- The clocks and calendar under the native core's `os` library, as its
--- host answers them. A call of one is the core's own library call, and
--- requiring this module loads nothing: it exists only on the core, for
--- `nupp.runtime.luatime`. Broken-down times are C's `struct tm` fields in
--- its order, from seconds to the daylight-saving flag, as C keeps them
--- (the month and the days of the week and year from 0, the year less
--- 1900, the flag negative when unknown).
local record timecalls
    --- The wall clock in whole seconds since the epoch, C's time(NULL).
    now: function(): integer

    --- The processor time this process has used, in seconds, as C's clock()
    --- over CLOCKS_PER_SEC.
    clock: function(): number

    --- Time `t` broken down, in UTC when `utc` is 1 and else local time: its
    --- nine fields, or nil when the system cannot represent it.
    parts: function(t: integer, utc: integer): {integer}?

    --- C's mktime of the nine `fields`, which it sets normalized: the time,
    --- or -1 when the system cannot represent it.
    make: function(fields: {integer}): integer

    --- strftime of the one conversion `spec` (`%` and Lua's option) for `t`
    --- broken down as `parts` breaks it: its text, or nil when the system
    --- cannot represent `t`.
    format: function(t: integer, utc: integer, spec: string): string?
end

local calls: timecalls
return calls
